From a331deca2399d0c5fbbbc1eff77a0d33133466ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lattice Bridge <bridge@lattice.local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:37:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] lattice: lattice-bridge builtin for native LAT issuance
 and burn

Adds programs/lattice-bridge (solana-lattice-bridge-program), a builtin
at Geuc2RbbzoWXSNYRyVDcjM5fZx6raKgf45y1bQr6aSzN gated by the new feature
enable_lattice_bridge_program (EX9XkmgKPffcEKpHpStcMDwFixLVV6RG94XN1i1WcdWi),
registered in BUILTINS without a Core BPF migration config.

- MintFromDeposit: M-of-N guardian threshold (Ed25519, ML-DSA-65 or
  hybrid, per guardian-set scheme) over the BRIDGE_SPEC wire-v1 DEPOSIT
  message; exact SCALE conversion; exactly-once via the
  ["minted", deployment, sequence] record PDA; per-epoch mint limit;
  deposit pause; credits the recipient and records +amount.
- BurnForWithdrawal: withdrawal pause; amount must be a whole source unit;
  moves lamports into the state PDA, debits them and records -amount;
  writes a LATBURN1 receipt at ["burn", deployment, sequence] with a
  monotonic sequence.
- Govern (kind 4): RotateGuardians (current threshold, epoch+1), SetPause,
  SetLimits, SetPauser, BindLatticeGenesis; strictly sequential nonce.
- Pause: optional pauser key may only pause.
- Attestation staging accounts (Init/Write/Verify/Close) so ML-DSA-65
  signatures can be verified across several transactions.

All signature checks and PDA derivations are compute-metered. Unaudited.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
